\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar recovers modestly after recent sell-off.   \b0\par\par\uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 11:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     HONG KONG, March 30 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar regained\par some lost ground against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday afternoon\par as players locked in profits after recent selling.\par     "There was some profit taking and we heard a U.S. name sold\par U.S. dollars against the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," one trader said.\par     The Hong Kong dollar        firmed to a four-day high of\par 7.7990 per U.S. dollar before settling at 7.7994/95 at 0927 GMT,\par compared with 7.7998/99 in late Asian trade on Tuesday.\par     The Hong Kong dollar was under pressure amid persistent\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 weakness in local stocks and a recent rebound in the U.S. dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 That prompted the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  late on Tuesday afternoon. It   \par \par \uc2 bought HK$390 million in exchange for U.S. dollars from banks.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     On Wednesday, Hong Kong stocks were steady and the blue-chip\par Hang Seng Index  ended up 0.10 percent.\par     Discounts on Hong Kong dollar forwards traded narrower\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 earlier in the day as the USD/HKD spot rate opened near the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 linked exchange rate, triggering fears of further fund outflows   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from the banking system, said a dealer at a Japanese bank.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     However, discounts on dollar forwards reversed course in the\par afternoon following a firmer local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     At 0930 GMT, the discount on one-year forwards          was\par quoted at 390/380 pips, versus 370 pips earlier in the day and\par Tuesday's close of 400/385 pips.\par     In the cash market, interbank rates edged off the morning\par highs and were taking a lead from a softening in dollar forwards\par rates, said a dealer at a local bank.\par     The one-month interbank rate was quoted at 2.58-2.60 percent,\par down from 2.62-2.65 percent in the morning, while the one-year\par softened to 3.28-3.30 percent from 3.30-3.35 percent.\par     However, dealers said interbank rates were likely to remain\par firm in the longer term on the prospect of higher interest rates\par in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and United States.\par     Recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 (HKMA) will reduce the aggregate balance - the sum of balances   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA - to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HK$3.85 billion after settlement on Thursday, its lowest level in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 five months. However, the balance is still significantly above   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its normal level of less than HK$1 billion.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BOC Hong Kong (2388.HK) Deputy Chief Executive Lam Yim Nam   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said on Wednesday he believed that Hong Kong could raise rates   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 again before the next U.S. Federal Reserve Open Market committee   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (FOMC) meeting in May if funds continue to flow out of the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banking system.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "As I keep on saying we look at this on a daily basis, on a   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 regular basis. You can't make a decision based on one days   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 activity. I think what the banks will do is probably have a look   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 over the course of the next two or three days to see what happens   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and then we'll take a decision on what to do next," David Eldon,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 chairman of HSBC (0005.HK), said on Wednesday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0927 GMT   At 0257 GMT   At 0923 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7994/95     7.7996/97     7.7998/99\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       - 68 / -63    - 70 / - 65   - 68 / - 63\par  Six-month         -170 / -160   -163 / -153   -170 / -160\par  One-year          -390 / -380   -385 / -365   -400 / -385\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         2.15 / 2.20   2.25 / 2.30   2.20 / 2.25\par  Three-month       2.74 / 2.76   2.75 / 2.80   2.70 / 2.75\par  Six-month         2.93 / 2.95   2.90 / 2.95   2.89 / 2.94\par  One-year          3.28 / 3.30   3.30 / 3.35   3.29 / 3.34\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050330e13u007vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
