\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar remains weak despite  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 10:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , March 16 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar remained\par weak against the greenback on Wednesday as investors continued to\par draw funds from the territory in search of higher yields\par elsewhere, prompting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in twice within 24\par hours to support the Hong Kong dollar. It bought HK$148 million\par in exchange for U.S. dollars from banks late on Wednesday,\par following the purchase of HK$780 million in London trade on\par Tuesday.\par     Under the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board system, the HKMA is committed to\par defending the pegged rate of HK$7.80 by buying Hong Kong dollars\par in exchange for U.S. dollars.\par     "The outflows were mainly due to interest rate differentials\par and a further decline in the aggregate balance, reflecting an\par imminent interest rate hike in Hong Kong," one dealer at a local\par bank said.\par  \par     Some dealers also said such speculative trades would push\par banks to raise rates.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Hong Kong interest rates usually move in tandem with U.S.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rates due to the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peg to the U.S. dollar, but   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banks here have ignored recent U.S. rate increases because the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 local banking system was awash with cash.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     However, excessive liquidity in the banking system has shrunk\par in recent months.\par     The latest move by the HKMA will reduce the aggregate balance\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 with the HKMA - to HK$4.748 billion after settlement on Friday,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its lowest level in five months, from HK$15.789 billion at the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 beginning of the year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  failed to strengthen after the HKMA   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . More fund outflows are expected," another dealer   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     At 0900 GMT the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7998/99\par against the greenback, just shy of its 7.80 pegged rate.\par     Hong Kong interbank rates rose and discounts on dollar\par forwards narrowed in the wake of fund outflows.\par     The one-month interbank rate firmed to 1.98-2.03 percent from\par Tuesday's close of 1.88-1.93 percent in Asian trade, while the\par one-year was at 2.94-2.99 percent versus 2.85-2.91 percent.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          narrowed to\par 560/540 pips from 615/595 pips late on Tuesday.\par     There has been growing speculation that local banks will have\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to raise saving deposit rates and prime lending rates soon after   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 many banks lifted their time deposit rates recently following a   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 decline in the aggregate balance and rising interbank rates.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A local news paper quoted Standard Chartered Bank's head of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 consumer banking, Tan Kong-khoon, as saying he expected to see an   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 interest rate increase in Hong Kong of between 0.25 and 0.375   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 percent after the Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) meeting.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The FOMC is expected to raise benchmark interest rates by   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 another 25 basis points at its March 22 meeting and to continue   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 to boost rates at least through the middle of the year.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Some dealers believed that banks will increase rates\par gradually to avoid derailing local economic growth.\par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0839 GMT   At 0300 GMT   At 0854 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7998/99     7.7997/98     7.7998/99\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -143 / -138   -150 / -145   -158 / -153\par  Six-month         -280 / -270   -293 / -283   -315 / -305\par  One-year          -560 / -540   -580 / -560   -615 / -595\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         1.20 / 1.30   1.20 / 1.25   1.20 / 1.30\par  Three-month       2.27 / 2.32   2.23 / 2.28   2.16 / 2.21\par  Six-month         2.54 / 2.59   2.50 / 2.55   2.43 / 2.50\par  One-year          2.94 / 2.99   2.90 / 2.95   2.85 / 2.91\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050316e13g003tn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
