\par\par \b \uc2 HK stocks down 1 pct by midday, Lenovo bucks trend.   \b0\par\par\uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 05:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     HONG KONG, March 10 (Reuters) - Hong Kong blue-chip stocks\par fell 1 percent by midday on Thursday with recent market darlings\par such as Chinese oil producer CNOOC Ltd. under pressure after\par another fall on Wall Street.\par     But China's top computer maker Lenovo Group Ltd. jumped 5.38\par percent to HK$2.45 after winning clearance from a U.S. national\par security committee to acquire IBM's personal computer business.\par     Investors are also waiting to hear from Hong Kong's unpopular\par leader Tung Chee-hwa, who is likely to announce his resignation\par this afternoon, sources told Reuters.\par     "The market will probably move up a little bit on the\par announcement, but that'll be short-lived. We're still facing the\par prospect of very drastic interest rate hikes in the short term,"\par said Alfred Chan, chief dealer at Cheer Pearl Investment Ltd.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Chan said worries about funds flowing out of the Hong Kong\par market were reignited on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had to repeatedly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to shore up the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which is pegged to the greenback.\par     By the midday recess, the benchmark Hang Seng index was 1.02\par percent, or 142.12 points, lower at 13,799.35, snapping a\par three-session rebound from a one-month low.\par  \par     Turnover at HK$11.5 billion ($1.5 billion) was slightly ahead\par of Wednesday's HK$11.3 billion.\par     On Wall Street, the Dow Jones industrial average fell for a\par third session, losing 0.98 percent to 10,805.62, while the Nasdaq\par Composite index slipped 0.59 percent to 2,061.29.\par     STOCKS TO WATCH:\par     - Hong Kong blue-chip conglomerate Swire Pacific Ltd. was\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 steady at HK$64 ahead of its full-year results. Hongkong Electric   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Holdings Ltd., also due to report its full-year results, was down   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0.57 percent at HK$34.90.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - China Shipping Container Lines rose 2.01 percent to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HK$3.80, extending Wednesday's 6.43 percent rally after Morgan   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stanley raised its earnings estimates for the firm and upgraded   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its rating to "overweight", driven by the firm's strong earnings.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Hutchison Telecommunications International Ltd. (HTIL) sank   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1.28 percent to HK$7.70 after it said it will pay US$120 million   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 for a 60 percent stake in a start-up cellular carrier in   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 fast-growing Indonesia. See for full story.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Dominant airline Cathay Pacific Airways Ltd., partly owned   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 by Swire, edged 0.35 percent lower to HK$14.15 after CSFB cut its   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 recommendation on the firm to "underperform" from "neutral" on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 concerns about rising fuel costs. It had risen 1.79 percent rise   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on Wednesday after better-than-expected second-half earnings.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - China top offshore oil and gas producer CNOOC Ltd.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 succumbed to profit-taking after jumping to a fresh high of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HK$4.625 in the previous session on the back of rising oil   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 prices. It fell 3.80 percent to HK$4.425. JP Morgan has raised   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 its earnings estimates for CNOOC and PetroChina on expectatons of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 higher long-term oil prices. PetroChina was down 1.51 percent at   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HK$4.90.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - Geely Automobile Holdings slid 1.92 percent to HK$0.51   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 after it reported a 44 percent fall in February volume sales from   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a month ago in its car manufacturing units due to fewer business   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 days last month to celebrate the Chinese New Year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050310e13a003v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
