\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar firms after recent fund outflows.   \b0\par\par\uc2 622 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 10:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, March 10 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar inched\par higher on Thursday after massive fund outflows the previous day\par prompted the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par support the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar was also taking a cue from the weakness\par of the greenback against regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par Expectations that Hong Kong's Chief Executive Tung Chee-hwa\par will finally announce his resignation at a press conference\par scheduled for 0930 GMT was having no appreciable effect on the\par market as few investors expect his departure will change the\par government's conservative fiscal stance.\par     "Hong Kong's economy has been recovering in the last 20\par months, I don't think his resignation will have any detrimental\par impact on the market," one trader said.\par  \par     "That he will resign is a known fact. So the impact will not\par be great," a Japanese bank dealer said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said they were far more concerned about the fund\par flows and interest rate policy than Tung's likely departure.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2           firmed to 7.7987 against the\par dollar in the afternoon before settling at 7.7993/94 at 0936 GMT,\par up from 7.7999/7.80 in late Asian trade on Wednesday.\par     "The market was tracking the dollar/Asians (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 )\par movements. There was also some dollar-selling after the London\par market entered," said the Japanese bank dealer.\par     The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) bought HK$2.418\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 billion in exchange for U.S. dollars from banks on Wednesday to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 support the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  amid accelerating arbitrage trade on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 speculation that local interest rates will soon be raised.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A fall in the aggregate balance, rising local interbank rates   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and expectations of continued rises in U.S. rates have increased   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pressure for Hong Kong banks' to raise interest rates, dealers   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The three-month interbank rate has risen to above 2 percent   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from around 0.8 percent in late January, reflecting the fact the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 market has priced in a near term interest rate hike," one trader   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 at a European bank said.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     In view of higher interbank rates, some small- and\par medium-size banks have raised their fixed deposit rates.\par     Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound and discounts\par widened in the afternoon following a firmer local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "There was some profit taking in the forwards market with the\par one-year hitting a high of -520/-530 pips in early trade," the\par Japanese bank dealer said.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          was trading at\par 600/580 pips by late afternoon, wider than Wednesday's close of\par 570/540 pips.\par     Hong Kong interbank rates came off from the morning highs\par after a firmer local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and a widening in forward\par discounts.\par     The one-month interbank rate was quoted at 1.88-1.91 percent\par versus 1.95-2.00 in the morning, while the three-month eased to\par 2.15-2.20 percent from 2.25-2.30 percent.\par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0827 GMT   At 0328 GMT   At 0940 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7993/94     7.7995/96     7.7998/7.80\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -155 / -150   -138 / -132   -155 / -145\par  Six-month         -310 / -330   -275 / -265   -295 / -280\par  One-year          -600 / -580   -560 / -540   -570 / -540\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         1.00 / 1.00   0.98 / 1.03   0.90 / 1.00\par  Three-month       2.15 / 2.20   2.25 / 2.30   2.16 / 2.21\par  Six-month         2.38 / 2.41   2.48 / 2.53   2.43 / 2.48\par  One-year          2.80 / 2.83   2.85 / 2.90   2.80 / 2.85\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050310e13a003e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
