\par\par \b \uc2 HK fund outflows trigger HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 11:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , March 9 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  interbank rates rose\par and discounts on dollar forwards rebounded from earlier lows late\par on Wednesday after persistent fund outflows triggered an\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) reported late on\par Wednesday that it had bought a total of HK$2.418 billion in\par exchange for U.S. dollars from banks in four separate moves to\par support the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Under the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board system, the HKMA is committed to\par defending the pegged rate of HK$7.80 by buying Hong Kong dollars\par in exchange for U.S. dollars.\par  \par     "The buy orders for U.S. dollars may be arbitrage trades,"\par said a dealer from a Japanese bank.\par     Another trader at a European bank said he noted some\par dollar-buying from Chinese-named banks.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been pressured because U.S. interest\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rates are higher than Hong Kong rates, enabling traders to earn   \f28 \par \par \uc2 an interest rate spread if they sell the Hong Kong dollar for   \par \par \uc2 U.S. dollars.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     At 0921 GMT, the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         was trading at 7.7999\par against the greenback, just shy of its 7.80 peg rate.\par     The one-month interbank rate rose to 1.90-1.95 percent from\par 1.63-1.68 percent after the massive fund outflows, while the\par one-year rate was at 2.80-2.85 percent versus 2.65-2.70 percent.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          narrowed to\par 570/540 pips, off the day's low of 670 pips, from Tuesday's close\par of 640/620 pips.\par     "I think banks may raise interest rates this week as the\par aggregate balance has been reduced quite a lot in recent months,"\par the European bank dealer said.\par     The latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the HKMA will reduce the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 aggregate balance - the sum of balances on clearing accounts   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 maintained by banks with the HKMA - to HK$5.541 billion after   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 settlement on Friday, its lowest level since late October, 2004.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong interest rates usually move in tandem with the U.S.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rates due to the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peg to the U.S. dollar, but   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banks here ignored recent U.S. rate increases because the local   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 banking system is awash in cash.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Since February, the HKMA has bought a cumulative HK$10.28   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 billion (US$1.32 billion) from banks, including Wednesday's   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Some dealers believed that banks will raise benchmark rates\par gradually to avoid derailing local economic growth.\par     "I think the banks will raise rate by 25 basis points each\par before the next FOMC meeting on March 22," the European bank\par dealer added.\par                    Close         Morning     