\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA continues buying HK dollars for the third day.   \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2005\par 02:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, Feb 3 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA), the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reported it bought HK$1.193 billion from banks in exchange for U.S. dollars in the offshore market overnight to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2  Since Monday, the HKMA has bought a total of HK$6.146 billion, including Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2  Under \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the HKMA is committed to defending the pegged rate of HK$7.8 by buying Hong Kong dollars in exchange for U.S. dollars.    \par \par \uc2  Real time information available on Reuters page  showed the transaction.    \par \par \uc2  At 0925 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7996/98 per U.S. dollar versus 7.7998/99 in late Asian trade on Wednesday.    \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has suffered selling pressure recently because U.S. interest rates are higher than Hong Kong rates, enabling traders to earn an interest rate spread if they sell Hong Kong dollars for U.S. dollars.    \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve raised its benchmark fed funds overnight bank lending rates by 25 basis points to 2.50 percent on Wednesday. But dealers are divided over whether Hong Kong banks will follow suit as there is still ample liquidity in the banking system.    \par \par \uc2  The aggregate balance - the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  - will be at HK$9.655 billion after settlement of recent outflows on Friday. It is still substantially higher than its normal level of HK$400-500 million.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050203e1230015s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
