\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA continues buying HK dlrs in offshore trade.   \b0\par\par\uc2 225 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 2005\par 02:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, Feb 2 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA), the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reported it bought HK$1.131 billion from banks in exchange for U.S. dollars in the offshore market overnight to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Under Hong Kong's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system, the HKMA is committed to defending the pegged rate of HK$7.8 by buying Hong Kong dollars in exchange for U.S. dollars.   \par \par \uc2 Real time information available on Reuters page showed the transaction.   \par \par \uc2 Since Monday, the HKMA has bought a total of HK$4.953 billion, including Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 At 0913 GMT, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was trading at 7.7998/99 per U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has suffered selling pressure recently because U.S. interest rates are higher than Hong Kong rates, enabling traders to earn an interest rate spread if they sell Hong Kong dollars for U.S. dollars.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve is widely expected to raise rates further later on Wednesday, but analysts are divided over whether Hong Kong banks will follow suit as there is ample liquidity in the banking system and loan demand remains soft.   \par \par \uc2 Weakness in the local dollar has also fuelled fears that investors are pulling speculative money from Hong Kong's stock market.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050202e122001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picsca