\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar weakens, short-term money remains tight.   \b0\par\par\uc2 582 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2004\par 10:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Dec 9 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar weakened on\par Thursday as the greenback retained its gains against major\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and after the latest round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong\par Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) on Wednesday to stem the local\par unit's strength.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         eased to a one-week low of 7.7762\par to the U.S. dollar before trading back to 7.7756/59 at 0920 GMT,\par down from 7.7702/04 in late Asian trade on Wednesday.\par  \par     One trader from a Japanese bank said there was some dollar\par buying after the London market opened.\par     "Some people are now buying U.S. dollars in anticipation that\par the funds which flowed into Hong Kong IPOs will soon return," the\par trader said.\par     Another dealer at a European bank said there was some\par technical dollar-buying due to the greenback's retracement.\par     The U.S. dollar rebounded for a second session against the\par yen  and the euro        on Thursday as traders and\par investors took profits after weeks of steep dollar declines.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In the interbank market, front-end liquidity remained tight\par with a large amount of funds tied up by recent IPO fever.\par     The retail portion of Air China Ltd's IPO was 83 times\par subscribed and has frozen up about HK$72.19 billion (US$9.25\par billion), market sources say.\par     The public share sale of Hong Kong Housing Authority's Link\par REIT, which ended on Thursday, is widely expected by the market\par to be hugely oversubscribed.\par     The overnight interbank rate was quoted at 2.50 percent by\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 late afternoon after hitting an intraday high of 4.0 percent. The   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one-week rate was trading at 2.25-2.50 percent, said a dealer   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from a local bank.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Rates are expected to remain choppy and liquidity will only   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ease after the two big IPOs debut in mid-December and the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 receiving banks clear the cheques," the dealer said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong dollar forwards were mixed. Shorter-dated forwards   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 moved in tandem with front-end interbank rates. The overnight and   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 tomorrow/next forwards were trading at a premium. Meanwhile,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 longer-dated forwards were trapped in narrow ranges.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile the HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 sold a total of HK$1.189 billion of U.S. dollar in offshore trade   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on Wednesday in two separate moves in a bid to curb the local   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's advance against the greenback.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 So far this week, the HKMA has sold a cumulative HK$1.671   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 billion. As a result, the aggregate balance - the sum of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - will rise to HK$15.83 billion after settlement on Friday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0920 GMT   At 0238 GMT   At 0859 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7756/59     7.7713/15     7.7703/05\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -368 / -358   -370 / -360   -355 / -350\par  Six-month         -730 / -720   -740 / -725   -735 / -720\par  One-year          -1340/-1320   -1355/-1335   -1360/-1340\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         2.50 / 2.50   3.50 / 3.75   1.00 / 1.25\par  Three-month       0.57 / 0.62   0.53 / 0.58   0.51 / 0.56\par  Six-month         0.70 / 0.75   0.73 / 0.78   0.66 / 0.71\par  One-year          1.13 / 1.18   1.00 / 1.15   1.08 / 1.13\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041209e0c9005ni\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
