\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr off morning lows on fund inflow stream.   \b0\par\par\uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 10:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Dec 7 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar ended\par little changed but off morning lows on Tuesday, with discounts on\par forwards widening on hopes of a further inflow of funds to the\par territory for upcoming IPOs.\par     "There was some dollar buying in early trade but then lack of\par follow-through action after the greenback fell below 103 yen,"\par one dealer at a local bank said.\par     Earlier in the day, the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in offshore trade\par on Monday to stem the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar's strength, and as the\par greenback regained some lost ground after a joint statement from\par European officials.\par     But the U.S. dollar weakened in the afternoon and touched an\par all-time low near $1.3470  and a 12-year low against\par sterling beyond $1.95 .\par     Dealers said greenback weakness, spurred by concerns about\par the U.S. current account and budget deficits, would continue to\par support Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  including the Hong Kong dollar.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         was trading at 7.7717/18 per U.S.\par dollar at 0911 GMT versus an intraday low of 7.7730 and little\par changed from 7.7715/17 in late Asian trade on Monday.\par     "Yesterday's inflow of funds was probably due to the IPOs. I\par think there will still be sporadic fund inflows but not massive\par ones because subscription for the biggest IPOs comes to an end\par later this week," said a dealer from a European bank.\par     The two large IPOs, Air China and the Hong Kong Housing\par Authority's Link property trust, are due to close on Wednesday\par and Thursday, respectively.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sold HK$482\par million of U.S. dollar in offshore trade on Monday. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of\par balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA\par -- to HK$14.621 billion after settlement on Wednesday.\par     Hong Kong interbank rates softened slightly and discounts on\par forwards widened on Tuesday given rising interbank liquidity\par after the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the HKMA.\par  \par     The discount on one-year forwards          widened to\par 1,410/1,390 pips from Monday's close of 1,370/1,340 pips.\par     Some dealers said forwards discounts would widen further if\par the U.S. Federal Reserve raises interest rates again next week\par and Hong Kong banks keep rates unchanged.\par     "I think there is a high possibility banks here will not\par track the Fed move given a high surplus in the aggregate\par balance," the local bank dealer said.\par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0917 GMT   At 0240 GMT   At 0830 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7717/18     7.7725/26     7.7716/17\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -385 / -380   -382 / -377   -373 / -363\par  Six-month         -775 / -760   -765 / -755   -750 / -735\par  One-year          -1410/-1390   -1390/-1370   -1370/-1340\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.37 / 0.62   0.65 / 0.70   0.65 / 0.75\par  Three-month       0.38 / 0.43   0.40 / 0.43   0.45 / 0.50\par  Six-month         0.58 / 0.63   0.60 / 0.64   0.63 / 0.68\par  One-year          1.02 / 1.07   1.05 / 1.08   1.08 / 1.13\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters contributor page .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041207e0c700798\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
