\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr eases after HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 ,greenback recovers.   \b0\par\par\uc2 464 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 04:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Dec 7 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar inched\par lower on Tuesday morning after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par (HKMA) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday to stem the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par strength, and as the greenback regained some lost ground after a\par joint statement from European officials.\par     "Yesterday's inflow of funds was probably due to the IPOs. I\par think there will still be sporadic fund inflows but not massive\par ones because the subscription for the biggest IPOs are coming to\par an end later this week," said a dealer from a European bank.\par     The two large IPOs, Air China and the Hong Kong Housing\par Authority's Link property trust, are due to close on Wednesday\par and Thursday, respectively.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sold HK$482\par million of U.S. dollar in offshore trade on Monday. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of\par balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA\par -- to HK$14.621 billion after settlement on Wednesday.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Dealers said the U.S. dollar rebound had added a little\par pressure on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The greenback gained some respite after the head of European\par    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and euro zone finance ministers said in a joint   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 statement that sharp moves in exchange rates were unwelcome and   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 they were closely monitoring swings.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong dollar exchange rate was trading at   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7.7725 against the greenback at 0312 GMT versus 7.7715/17 in late   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian trade on Monday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong interbank rates softened slightly and discounts on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 forwards widened on Tuesday morning given rising interbank   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 liquidity after the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the HKMA.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The one-week interbank rate was quoted at 1.00-1.06 percent,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 compared with 1.06-1.12 percent on Monday. Short-term interbank   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rates have risen recently as demand for IPOs put a squeeze on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bank funds.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The one-year interbank rate eased to 1.05-1.08 percent from\par Monday's 1.08-1.03 percent.\par     Meanwhile, the discount on one-year forwards          widened\par to 1,390/1,370 pips from Monday's close of 1,370/1,340 pips.\par                    Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0240 GMT   At 0830 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7725/26     7.7716/17\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -382 / -377   -373 / -363\par  Six-month         -765 / -755   -750 / -735\par  One-year          -1390/-1370   -1370/-1340\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.65 / 0.70   0.65 / 0.75\par  Three-month       0.40 / 0.43   0.45 / 0.50\par  Six-month         0.60 / 0.64   0.63 / 0.68\par  One-year          1.05 / 1.08   1.08 / 1.13\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \