\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr eases as U.S. dlr bolstered by ECB comments.   \b0\par\par\uc2 528 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2004\par 10:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     HONG KONG, Nov 9 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar edged lower\par on Tuesday as the greenback regained some lost ground after\par supportive comments from European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         fell to a session low of 7.7783 per\par U.S. dollar before trading back to 7.7763/65 at 0905 GMT, weaker\par than 7.7736/37 in late Asian trade on Monday.\par     "The dollar traded to 105.70 yen, and remarks from European\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials helped the U.S. dollar," said a dealer\par from a Japanese bank.\par     The pause in the dollar's downtrend came after European\par    \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Jean-Claude Trichet warned against the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 euro's rapid rise on Monday. ECB Governing Council member Guy   \par \par \uc2 Quaden followed Trichet's comments, telling a Belgian newspaper   \par \par \uc2 that further appreciation of the euro would be undesirable.   \par \par \uc2 However, some dealers said the dollar's downtrend was not yet   \par \par \uc2 over and it would remain under pressure by concerns about the   \par \par \uc2 U.S. budget and current account deficits.   \par \par \uc2 Another trader from a local bank said the fall in the local   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was due to some players covering short dollar positions   \par \par \uc2 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on   \par \par \uc2 Monday to stem the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise against the greenback.   \par \par \uc2 The discount on one-year forwards was quoted at   \par \par \uc2 1,365/1,350 pips by late afternoon, narrower than Monday's close   \par \par \uc2 of 1,410/1,380 pips.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve is holding its policy-setting   \par \par \uc2 meeting on Wednesday. Dealers said the market has already priced   \par \par \uc2 in a 25 basis points rise in rates but they are are anxious to   \par \par \uc2 see the accompanying statement, which could hint at the future   \par \par \uc2 pace of monetary tightening.   \par \par \uc2 "People previously thought the Fed would pause in raising   \par \par \uc2 rates in December ... but the strong U.S. employment data for   \par \par \uc2 October has raised the prospects of another rate increase next   \par \par \uc2 month," one trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Hong Kong tends to track U.S. rate moves because of the   \par \par \uc2 territory's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  peg to the U.S. dollar. But Hong Kong banks   \par \par \uc2 are unlikely to follow the Fed's lead this time due to a banking   \par \par \uc2 system awash with funds.   \par \par \uc2 The aggregate balance, the sum of balances on clearing   \par \par \uc2 accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA, will rise to   \par \par \uc2 HK$14.118 billion on Wednesday.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0855 GMT   At 0305 GMT   At 0906 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7765/66     7.7760/62     7.7736/37\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -405 / -400   -410 / -400   -427 / -422\par  Six-month         -760 / -750   -765 / -755   -795 / -785\par  One-year          -1365/-1350   -1375/-1355   -1410/-1380\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.03 / 0.03   0.02 / 0.05   0.02 / 0.03\par  Three-month       0.20 / 0.23   0.1