\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr edges lower as USD short covering persists.   \b0\par\par\uc2 413 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2004\par 04:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Nov 9 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar edged lower\par on Tuesday morning as some players continued to cover short\par dollar positions after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA)\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday to stem the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise against\par the greenback.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         was trading at 7.7760/62 per U.S.\par dollar at 0302 GMT, easier than 7.7736/37 in late Asian trade on\par Monday.\par     Meanwhile, the discount on one-year forwards\par narrowed to 1,375/1,355 pips from Monday's close of 1,410/1,380\par pips.\par     One dealer from a local bank said the greenback rebounded and\par a narrowing discount on yuan non-deliverable forwards had added\par pressure on the Hong Kong dollar.\par     The dollar edged up from a record low against the euro\par on Tuesday after comments from European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President\par Jean-Claude Trichet, who said the euro's recent rise was "brutal"\par and unwelcome.\par  \par     The dollar also gained versus the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par 105.57/60 yen  versus 105.48 in late U.S. trade.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There was some technical adjustment before the Federal\par Reserve's meeting," another trader at a local bank said.\par     "Players are watching out for the Fed's accompanying\par statement for hints on the pace of future rate rises."\par     The U.S. Federal Reserve is holding its policy-setting\par meeting on Wednesday. Dealers said the market has already priced\par in a 25 basis points rise in rates.\par     Hong Kong tends to track U.S. rate moves because of the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par territory's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  peg to the U.S. dollar. But Hong Kong banks\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are unlikely to follow the Fed's lead this time due to a banking\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par system awash with funds.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The aggregate balance, the sum of balances on clearing\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA, will rise to\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0305 GMT   At 0906 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7760/62     7.7736/37\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -410 / -400   -427 / -422\par  Six-month         -765 / -755   -795 / -785\par  One-year          -1375/-1355   -1410/-1380\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.02 / 0.05   0.02 / 0.03\par  Three-month       0.19 / 0.24   0.12 / 0.17\par  Six-month         0.42 / 0.47   0.30 / 0.35\par  One-year          0.92 / 0.97   0.81 / 0.86\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters contributor page .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041109e0b9004bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
