\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr sheds some early gains on USD short covering.   \b0\par\par\uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2004\par 10:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Nov 8 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar trimmed\par some of its earlier gains late on Monday as some players covered\par short U.S. dollar positions after the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) to stem the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par advance against the greenback.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         was trading at 7.7736/37 per U.S.\par dollar at 0906 GMT, off a morning high of 7.7700, but still\par firmer than 7.7750/55 in late Asian trade on Friday, said a\par dealer from a Japanese bank.\par     Meanwhile, the discount on one-year forwards          hit a\par morning's low of 1,480 pips and rebounded slightly to 1,410/1,380\par pips in late afternoon trade but still wider than Friday's close\par of 1,320/1,300 pips.\par     "The market has been volatile in recent weeks with some\par short-term trading. I think some people are taking profits after\par the recent selling spree on the U.S. dollar against the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," another trader at a local bank said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose to its highest level against the\par greenback since mid-February in early morning trade, helped by a\par broadly weaker U.S. dollar and heightened speculation about a\par revaluation of the Chinese yuan.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sold\par HK$1.554 billion of U.S. dollars on Monday morning. The\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum of\par balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA\par -- to HK$14.118 billion after settlement on Wednesday.\par     The Hong Kong dollar is pegged at 7.80 to the U.S. dollar but\par it is often seen as a proxy for the Chinese yuan as the two\par economies become more closely integrated.\par     Some dealers said the spot rate (the U.S. dollar against the\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) was still under heavy pressure as the market has\par been awash with concerns about internal and external U.S.\par deficits, which have been a key driver of dollar weakness.\par  \par     In the cash market, interbank rates remained low in the face\par of a higher aggregate balance.\par     Dealers said an expanding aggregate balance was boosting\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 speculation that Hong Kong banks will cut interest rates despite   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 market expectations that the Federal Reserve will lift its   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 short-term rates by 25 basis points at a Nov. 10 meeting.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0906 GMT   At 0232 GMT   At 0829 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7736/37     7.7706/08     7.7727/28\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -427 / -422   -435 / -432   -422 / -412\par  Six-month         -795 / -785   -825 / -810   -760 / -745\par  One-year          -1410/-1380   -1470/-1440   -1320/-1300\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.02 / 0.03   0.01 / 0.04   0.01 / 0.04\par  Three-month       0.12 / 0.17   0.08 / 0.13   0.13 / 0.18\par  Six-month         0.30 / 0.35   0.23 / 0.28   0.34 / 0.39\par  One-year          0.81 / 0.86   0.77 / 0.82   0.81 / 0.86\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041108e0b800cqg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
