\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr a touch softer, range trading seen.   \b0\par\par\uc2 427 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2004\par 05:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Oct 26 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar was a tad\par softer on Tuesday morning after aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday afternoon to stem the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise against the greenback.\par  \par     Discounts on Hong Kong dollar forwards also rebounded\par slightly from Monday's low.\par     "People who shorted the U.S. dollar or went long on the Hong\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2  Kong dollar on Monday were taking profits in view of a slight    \par \par \uc2  retreat for the yen and euro in early trade," said a dealer from    \par \par \uc2  a European bank.    \par \par \uc2  Japan said it would take action if the dollar falls too    \par \par \uc2  quickly against the yen, Japanese Vice Finance Minister for    \par \par \uc2  International Affairs Hiroshi Watanabe said on Monday, helping    \par \par \uc2  the dollar to pare some losses against the yen.    \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2   hit a session low of 7.7790 per    \par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar before trading back to 7.7782/83 by 0223 GMT, versus    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Discounts on one-year forwards          were trading at\par 1,050/1,020 pips, compared with Monday's low of 1,070 pips.\par     However, some dealers said the market was likely to remain\par volatile and focused on the dollar movement.\par     Recent high oil prices, mixed U.S. economic data and a\par widening U.S. current account deficit have weighed on the\par greenback.\par     In the cash market, interbank rates fell in the face of a\par rise in the aggregate balance after the HKMA sold HK$3.113\par billion on Monday afternoon to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     As a result, the aggregate balance -- the sum of balances on\par clearing accounts maintained by banks with the HKMA -- will rise\par to HK$8.635 billion after settlement on Wednesday.\par     The six-month interbank rate eased to 0.57-0.62 percent from\par Monday's close of 0.61-0.66 percent. The one-year rate was at\par 1.00-1.05 percent, down from 1.03-1.08 percent on Monday.\par                    Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0223 GMT   At 0936 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7782/83     7.7804/06\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -330 / -320   -330 / -320\par  Six-month         -625 / -605   -610 / -590\par  One-year          -1050/-1020   -1060/-1010\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.25 / 0.30   0.15 / 0.25\par  Three-month       0.40 / 0.45   0.38 / 0.43\par  Six-month         0.57 / 0.62   0.61 / 0.66\par  One-year          1.00 / 1.05   1.03 / 1.08\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters contributor page .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041026e0aq002e6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
