\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar touch softer, US dlr weakness supports.   \b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2004\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Oct 21 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar edged\par back towards its peg rate only slightly on Thursday after\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) late on\par Wednesday to counter its strength against a broadly weaker U.S.\par dollar.\par     After shuffling between 7.7854 and 7.7875 per U.S. dollar\par on Thursday, the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   traded at 7.7860/61 at\par 0912 GMT.\par     That was not far from Wednesday's high of 7.7850 which had\par prompted the HKMA to sell HK$779 million to weaken the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The HK dollar is pegged at 7.80 per U.S. dollar.\par     "Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were supported by the general weakness in\par the U.S. dollar. The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rebounded from the\par morning's low due to a softer dollar/yen," said a dealer at a\par European bank.\par  \par     The U.S. dollar fell to a four-month low against the yen on\par Thursday.\par     The Hong Kong dollar has traded slightly stronger than its\par pegged rate in recent weeks on speculation of a possible\par revaluation in the Chinese yuan .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is often seen as a proxy for the Chinese\par yuan as the two economies become more closely integrated.\par     Hong Kong dollar forwards fell further on Thursday, with\par the discount on one-year contracts  widening to 870/850\par pips from Wednesday's close of 800/790 pips.\par     "The discount on one-year forwards broke 765 pips, the\par lowest level in early January, on Wednesday and it immediately\par triggered stop-loss selling," a trader said.\par     In the cash market, interbank rates fell across the board\par after a rise in the aggregate balance.\par     The one-month interbank rate was quoted at 0.50-0.54\par percent, down from Wednesday's 0.63-0.68 percent.\par     Hong Kong financial markets will be closed on Friday for\par the Chung Yeung Festival, or grave-sweeping, holiday.\par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0912 GMT   At 0301 GMT   At 0857 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7960/61     7.7863/64     7.7851/52\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -263 / -258   -252 / -247   -238 / -233\par  Six-month         -490 / -480   -475 / -465   -455 / -445\par  One-year          -870 / -850   -845 / -825   -800 / -790\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.25 / 0.30   0.25 / 0.23   0.25 / 0.30\par  Three-month       0.54 / 0.59   0.82 / 0.87   0.83 / 0.88\par  Six-month         0.90 / 0.92   0.96 / 1.01   0.98 / 1.03\par  One-year          1.25 / 1.30   1.30 / 1.35   1.35 / 1.40\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041021e0al004zy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
