\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ Hong Kong Dollar Rises To 31-Wk High On China Yuan Talk  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Steven Vames  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2004\par 02:06\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2004, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The Hong Kong dollar surged versus its U.S. counterpart Friday, buoyed by renewed speculation that China is nearing a plan to revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it faces more pressure from the Bush Administration.  \par \par \uc2 The speculation about China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy re-emerged following reports that President George W. Bush had discussed the issue, amongst others, via telephone Thursday with Chinese President Hu Jintao. In recent months Chinese officials have reiterated their long-standing intention to loosen their tightly-controlled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy - which acts as a defacto peg versus the dollar - at some point, but have given no specific details and no timeline for such a move.  \par \par \uc2 The yuan's exchange rate is almost entirely government-controlled and gyrates in a narrow band with a central point of around 8.28 yuan against the dollar. The Hong-Kong dollar is also pegged to the U.S. dollar under a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  board system in which the entire monetary base is backed with U.S. dollars, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can occasionally deviate from that value.  \par \par \uc2 In late New York trading, the U.S. dollar was fetching HK$7.7815, compared to HK$7.7962 when trading opened. It was the lowest level for the dollar versus the Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late February.  \par \par \uc2 During London trade, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to resist upward pressure on the Hong Kong dollar. The HKMA sold a total of HK$1.557 billion, buying around US$199.9 million.  \par \par \uc2 Ali Rada, of Radaforex, an independent interdealer broker in New York, said the Hong Kong dollar's surge could also be linked to the pending initial public offering of China Power International Development Ltd. (2380.HK), which is expected to make a strong debut on the Hong Kong stock exchange next week.  \par \par \uc2 Any revaluation of the yuan is widely seen as a positive for the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including Hong Kong's dollar. Under that theory, other Asian governments would be more prone to allow their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate if the yuan was also appreciating against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Though the Chinese government has given no specific plans for any revaluation, markets have recently taken rumors seriously as rhetoric from the Bush Administration has heated up ahead of the U.S. presidential election.  \par \par \uc2 Market watchers said that while speculators are placing bets based on the rumors, most analysts are dismissing the possibility of a near-term revaluation.  \par \par \uc2 'This is a very political issue, and it's being taken seriously,' said Tetsu Hisa Hayashi, \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Manager at Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi in New York. 'But I have to say it is not so realistic. We think China would have given some information after last week's (Group of Seven) meeting if they did have near-term plans.'  \par \par \uc2 For the first time, China was a guest at the meeting of finance ministers from Group of Seven leading industrialzed nations last week in Washington.  \par \par \uc2 The rise in the Hong Kong dollar follows some similar action in related markets. China's yuan rose Friday in the offshore forwards market on the same news of Bush's conversation with Hu Jintao.  \par \par \uc2 In the Asian session, in the freely traded market for nondeliverable forwards, the dollar's one-year discount widened to 2475/2375, according to a late afternoon quote from Prebon Yamane, from 2150/2080 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 -Steven Vames; Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-5063; steven.vames@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 (Jeff Meyer in Shanghai contributed to this report)  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020041011e0ab0002v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
