\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr eases after HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  last week.   \b0\par\par\uc2 468 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2004\par 11:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Oct 11 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar edged\par lower on Monday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA)\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  late on Friday to stem the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise against the\par U.S. dollar.\par     "There was limited follow-through U.S. dollar selling today\par after the HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week," said a dealer from a\par French bank.\par     The Hong Kong dollar surged to its highest level on Friday\par since the end of February on mounting speculation that China\par could soon allow its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate against the U.S.\par dollar.\par     As a result, the HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at around 7.7850 on Friday\par afternoon by selling HK$1.557 billion for U.S. dollars in a bid\par to curb the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will lift the aggregate balance -- the sum\par of balances on clearing accounts maintained by the banks with the\par HKMA -- to HK$4.79 billion on Tuesday from Monday's HK$3.233\par billion.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     At 0822 GMT on Monday the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         was trading\par at 7.7915/16 versus its opening at 7.7860/70 per U.S. dollar, and\par below its 7.80 peg to the U.S. dollar.\par     But dealers said U.S. dollar weakness and persistent\par speculation on a Chinese yuan revaluation, would lend support to\par the Hong Kong dollar and other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "The market is in consolidation, but I think it will remain\par choppy before the U.S. presidential election," another trader at\par a European bank said.\par     The greenback fell to a four-week low against the yen and\par held near a recent one-week low versus the euro on Monday after\par weak U.S. jobs data fanned questions about future interest rate\par hikes in the United States.\par     Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound, tracking the\par movement in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and yuan non-deliverable forwards\par (NDFs), dealers said.\par  \par     The discount on one-year forwards          opened at 730/710\par pips but pulled back to 690/670 pips by late afternoon.\par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0811 GMT   At 0255 GMT   At 0842 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7910/12     7.7914/15     7.7908/10\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -200 / -195   -205 / -200   -182 / -177\par  Six-month         -385 / -375   -390 / -380   -360 / -345\par  One-year          -690 / -675   -700-/ -685   -670 / -650\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         1.00 / 1.25   1.00 / 1.06   1.25 / 1.40\par  Three-month       1.00 / 1.02   0.98 / 1.03   1.10 / 1.12\par  Six-month         1.14 / 1.16   1.15 / 1.20   1.26 / 1.28\par  One-year          1.48 / 1.50   1.49 / 1.54   1.62 / 1.65\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA000002