\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr pulls back from highs after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 412 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2004\par 05:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Oct 11 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar pulled\par back from recent highs on Monday morning after the territory's de\par facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  late on Friday to stem the local\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's advance, dealers said.\par     The Hong Kong dollar exchange rate        was trading at\par 7.7925 at 0306 GMT, pulling back from Friday's high of about\par 7.7815 hit in New York trade, and below its 7.80 peg to the U.S.\par dollar.\par     "The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stabilised this morning amid fears of\par further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA),"\par said a dealer from a Japanese bank.\par     The Hong Kong dollar surged to its highest level on Friday\par since the end of February on mounting speculation that China\par could soon allow its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to appreciate against the U.S.\par dollar.\par     The HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at around 7.7850 on Friday afternoon by\par selling HK$1.557 billion for U.S. dollars in a bid to curb the\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The move by the HKMA will lift the aggregate balance -- the\par sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by the banks with\par the HKMA -- to HK$4.79 billion on Tuesday from Monday's HK$3.233\par billion.\par     Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound. They opened wider\par on the back of lower U.S. bond yields after weak U.S. jobs data\par on Friday and on the yuan revaluation talk.\par     "Hong Kong dollar forwards will continue to track the\par movement of yuan NDFs. The one-year NDFs were trading at around\par 2,600 points this morning from 2,500 points on Friday," another\par trader from a European bank said.\par     At 0330 GMT, the discount on one-year Hong Kong dollar\par forwards  was trading at 700/685 pips versus Friday's low\par of 710 pips, the dealer said.\par  \par                    Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0255 GMT   At 0842 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7914/15     7.7908/10\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -205 / -200   -182 / -177\par  Six-month         -390 / -380   -360 / -345\par  One-year          -700-/ -685   -670 / -650\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         1.00 / 1.06   1.25 / 1.40\par  Three-month       0.98 / 1.03   1.10 / 1.12\par  Six-month         1.15 / 1.20   1.26 / 1.28\par  One-year          1.49 / 1.54   1.62 / 1.65\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041011e0ab003h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
