\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr recovers from recent lows on profit taking.   \b0\par\par\uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 September 2004\par 05:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Sept 2 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar recovered\par slightly from recent lows against the U.S. unit on Thursday\par morning amid some profit-taking on the greenback and in the wake\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par  \par     "There was some profit taking after a recent sell-off on\par arbitrage trades," one dealer said.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         strengthened to 7.7997/98 per U.S.\par dollar at 0219 GMT from 7.7999/7.80 late on Wednesday.\par     The HKMA, the city's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , bought a total of\par HK$2.73 billion from banks during onshore and offshore trading\par hours on Wednesday.\par     Under Hong Kong's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board system, the HKMA is\par committed to defending the pegged rate of HK$7.80 by buying Hong\par Kong dollars in exchange for U.S. dollars.\par     The latest moves by the HKMA will further reduce the\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2  aggregate balance - the sum of balances on clearing accounts    \par \par \uc2  maintained by banks with the HKMA - to HK$4.388 billion after    \par \par \uc2  the settlement of capital outflows on Friday.    \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has suffered selling pressure in recent    \par \par \uc2  months because U.S. interest rates are higher than Hong Kong    \par \par \uc2  rates, enabling traders to earn an interest rate spread if they    \par \par \uc2  sell Hong Kong dollars for U.S. dollars.    \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve has raised its benchmark funds rate    \par \par \uc2  by a total of 50 basis points in recent months but Hong Kong    \par \par \uc2  banks have left lending rates unchanged on lacklustre loan growth    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Some local banks increased savings rates in early August but\par only by a fraction.\par     Since July 16, the HKMA has bought a cumulative HK$31.126\par billion (US$3.99 billion) from the market.\par     The continuous outflow of funds has tightened bank liquidity,\par pushing up Hong Kong interbank rates and narrowing the discounts\par on Hong Kong dollar forwards.\par     "Arbitrage plays are expected to persist until local\par interbank interest rates rise in line with their U.S.\par counterparts," another trader from a local bank said.\par     The local three-month interbank rate was quoted at 0.85-0.90\par percent on Thursday, while the three-month U.S. interbank rate\par was at 1.78 percent.\par     Meanwhile, discounts on one-year forwards          narrowed\par to 425/410 pips from Wednesday's 450/430 pips.\par                    Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0250 GMT   At 0856 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7997/98     7.7999/7.80\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -179 / -174   -188 / -183\par  Six-month         -310 / -300   -320 / -310\par  One-year          -425 / -410   -450 / -430\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.06 / 0.09   0.03 / 0.08\par  Three-month       0.85 / 0.90   0.78 / 0.83\par  Six-month         1.11 / 1.16   1.08 / 1.13\par  One-year          1.63 / 1.70   1.62 / 1.67\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040902e0920030d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscal