\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar rebounds on profit taking, outlook murky.   \b0\par\par\uc2 668 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 August 2004\par 11:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Aug 5 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar\par strengthened above its peg against the U.S. unit on Thursday as\par some players booked profits after a recent heavy sell-off and in\par the wake of HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA), the territory's de\par facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , bought a total of HK$3.647 billion from banks\par during onshore and offshore trading hours on Wednesday.\par     Under Hong Kong's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board system, the HKMA is\par committed to defending the pegged rate of HK$7.8 by buying Hong\par Kong dollars in exchange for U.S. dollars.\par     The move by the HKMA will reduce the aggregate balance -- the\par sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks with the\par HKMA -- to HK$7.531 billion after the settlement of the capital\par outflow on Friday.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         shuffled between 7.7995 and 7.7998\par per U.S. dollar throughout the day and traded at 7.7996/97 at\par 0912 GMT, slightly firmer than 7.7999/7.80 in late Asian trade on\par Wednesday.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The Hong Kong dollar will remain weak along with a further\par decline in the aggregate balance ... the HKD failed to strengthen\par above 7.7995, reflecting demand for U.S. dollars in arbitrage\par plays," one dealer said.\par     Some dealers said if the differential between Hong Kong and\par U.S. interest rates remains large, arbitrage trades will continue\par and the aggregate balance could fall to a "negative" value.\par     A negative aggregate balance implies there will not be enough\par liquidity in the market for banks to settle their accounts,\par forcing them to borrow from the HKMA's discount window.\par     "If a 'negative' balance occurs, Hong Kong interbank rates\par may rise to higher levels than U.S. rates. Then arbitrage\par activities will be dissipated," one trader at a European bank\par said.\par     A flood of money entered the territory late last year due to\par a weak U.S. dollar, a rebound in the local economy and on\par speculation about a revaluation of China's yuan.\par     But there has been a reversal of fund flows in recent months\par on China's measures to cool its economy, expectations of rising\par U.S. interest rates and lacklustre local stocks.\par  \par     Total purchases of Hong Kong dollars by the HKMA between\par April 30 to August 4 have reached about HK$47.162 billion.\par     Although the aggregate balance has been declining from a peak\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 of HK$54.665 billion at the end of April, it is still   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 significantly above its normal level of less than HK$1 billion   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 before the capital inflows last year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound as players booked   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 profits before key U.S. payrolls data slated for Friday, said a   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dealer from a local bank.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The discount on one-year forwards was trading at   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 370/350 pips versus a morning high of 300 pips and Wednesday's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 close of 350/330 pips.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday's U.S. jobs report will be the last major data to be   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 released before the Federal Reserve's policy-setting meeting on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 10, when the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is expected to raise   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 interest rates by another 25 basis points.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0855 GMT   At 0245 GMT   At 0845 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7996/97     7.7997/98     7.7999/7.80\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -157 / -152   -145 / -140   -150 / -145\par  Six-month         -265 / -255   -245 / -235   -243 / -233\par  One-year          -370 / -350   -340 / -320   -350 / -330\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.12 / 0.12   0.09 / 0.11   0.06 / 0.09\par  Three-month       0.88 / 0.93   0.95 / 1.00   0.90 / 0.95\par  Six-month         1.24 / 1.28   1.30 / 1.37   1.26 / 1.31\par  One-year          1.83 / 1.85   1.87 / 1.93   1.85 / 1.90\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040805e085001o5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
