\par\par \b \uc2 HK shares end slightly lower but retailers rise.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Hunt  \par \uc2 656 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2004\par 10:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, July 26 (Reuters) - Hong Kong's leading share index dropped a slight 0.27 percent on Monday, but retailers rose on hopes that they will win back some pricing power soon as the territory's six-year deflationary spiral comes to an end.  \par \par \uc2 China plays such as cement maker Anhui Conch fell on fears that corporate earnings would be hurt by measures to rein in the country's booming economy.  \par \par \uc2 The Hang Seng Index , which groups 33 blue-chip stocks, ended down 33.16 points at 12,319.83. Investor confidence was hurt after the U.S. benchmark Dow Jones industrial average fell below the key 10,000-point level.  \par \par \uc2 Turnover was HK$7.9 billion, making it this year's lightest day of trade, according to Reuters data.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday also weighed on sentiment, indicating that more funds are leaving Hong Kong's equity market.  \par \par \uc2 Retailers such as Bossini International Ltd (0592.HK) jumped after the government said after the market close on Friday that Hong Kong prices were little changed in June from the previous month against a year earlier.  \par \par \uc2 "People think deflation is coming to an end," said Kenny Tang, associate director at Tung Tai Securities.  \par \par \uc2 Basic clothing retailer Bossini jumped 11.46 percent to HK$2.675, while women's clothing chain Moiselle International Ltd. (0130.HK) jumped 18.94 percent to HK$1.57 and Veeko International (1171.HK) climbed 13.82 percent to HK$0.28.  \par \par \uc2 But some brokers cautioned that trade on these second liners was speculative.  \par \par \uc2 Deflation robs companies of the ability to raise prices.  \par \par \uc2 Blue-chips were mixed. Bank of East Asia Ltd. (0023.HK) was up 0.88 percent at HK$22.85. It is forecast to report robust results on Friday, kicking off what is expected to be a strong first-half earnings season for Hong Kong companies.  \par \par \uc2 Cathay Pacific Airways Ltd (0293.HK) slipped 1.42 percent to HK$13.90 as investors speculated that a new air services agreement between China and the United States, signed over the weekend, could hurt Hong Kong-based airlines.  \par \par \uc2 The deal, which allows U.S. carriers greater access to Chinese cities, could result in less traffic being funnelled through Hong Kong, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 CHINA PLAYS  \par \par \uc2 The Hang Seng China Enterprise Index , which groups Chinese firms listed here, dropped 1.09 percent to 4,301.64.  \par \par \uc2 China's largest cement maker Anhui Conch Cement Co. Ltd. (0914.HK) fell 2.44 percent to HK$8 after a Hong Kong newspaper quoted a company executive as saying its cement prices had declined by 20 percent in May and June against the first quarter this year.  \par \par \uc2 The executive attributed the decline to China's economic cooling measures.  \par \par \uc2 "They'll show excellent earnings growth for this half but it's concerns over future earnings that's affecting sentiment," said Alex Tang, research director at Core Pacific-Yamaichi International.  \par \par \uc2 Jiangxi Copper (0358.HK) fell 3.92 percent to HK$3.675, while Angang New Steel Co. Ltd. (0347.HK) shed 4.07 percent to HK$2.95.  \par \par \uc2 The China Securities Journal said on Monday the country's consumer inflation was likely to exceed five percent in the year through July. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said earlier this year that China may need to raise interest rates if inflation hits five percent.  \par \par \uc2 Beijing Capital Land Ltd. (2868.HK) rose 3.76 percent to HK$1.93 after its proposed China domestic share issue was rejected by Chinese regulators. The news removed fears of a share dilution.  \par \par \uc2 However, some traders said overall sentiment remained optimistic with the Hang Seng ending off session lows.  \par \par \uc2 "There's strong support at the 12,000-to 12,200-points level, so I am quite confident," said Peter Lai, sales director at DBS Vickers Securities.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040726e07q000wi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
