\par\par \b \uc2 HK stocks end 0.60 pct lower, China plays sag.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Joyce Li  \par \uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2004\par 10:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG, July 22 (Reuters) - Hong Kong stocks fell 0.60 percent on Thursday but still managed to hold above the key 12,300 points level after worries over slowing corporate earnings growth dragged Wall Street lower.  \par \par \uc2 The benchmark Hang Seng Index ended down 74.90 points at 12,320.21 after racking up gains of 270 points on Wednesday. Turnover was light at HK$9.6 billion (US$1.23 billion) - down from HK$14.5 billion on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 China plays suffered heavier losses than the broader market. The H-share index of Hong Kong-listed Chinese-registered firms fell 1.28 percent to 4,379.10, after running into stubborn resistance at the 4,400 level in the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 UBS said that a soft landing for China's economy would be insufficient to spur the sector further. It said a slowdown would not be enough to stem overinvestment and overcapacity, which have already spawned a poor industrial structure in the country.  \par \par \uc2 "The sector came under heavy selling pressure because news that the country may engineer a soft landing had overpowered China plays way too much in the past few sessions," said Alex Wong, a research director at Rexcapital Asset Management.  \par \par \uc2 Most blue chips ended in negative territory, led by tech plays after the U.S. tech board tumbled more than two percent.  \par \par \uc2 Ports-to-telecom conglomerate Hutchison Whampoa Ltd. (0013.HK), an index heavyweight, dipped 0.93 percent to HK$53.50. Local newspapers said Japanese electronics giant NEC Corp. is interested in buying stakes in the planned listing of Hutchison's emerging markets telecoms business.  \par \par \uc2 Other index majors also weighed on the market. China Mobile (Hong Kong) Ltd. (0941.HK) slipped 0.65 percent to HK$23.10 while HSBC Holdings Plc. (0005.HK) (HSBA.L) lost 0.43 percent to HK$116.  \par \par \uc2 China plays sagged, led by power firms on fears that high coal prices would hit their margins. Datang International Power Generation (0991.HK) lost 3.01 percent to HK$6.45 while Huadian Power (1071.HK) fell 2.375 percent to HK$2.375.  \par \par \uc2 FUND OUTFLOW FEARS  \par \par \uc2 Worries that more funds may leave Hong Kong also curbed investor sentiment.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been pressured in recent weeks after the U.S. raised interest rates at the end of June. Hong Kong banks left their rates unchanged, making U.S. dollar denominated investments more attractive.  \par \par \uc2 Market players have speculated funds may leave Hong Kong given the interest rate differential and the prospect that the spread may widen if the U.S. lifts rates further in August.  \par \par \uc2 But dealers dismissed worries of another meltdown reminiscent of the 1997 Asian financial crisis. They said there were no signs of unusually large short stock positions and that the outflow of funds from Hong Kong was merely arbitrage trade.  \par \par \uc2 During the Asian financial crisis, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the stock and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to foil speculators who had simultaneously attacked the Hong Kong dollar and taken short positions in stocks and futures to benefit from falling stock prices.  \par \par \uc2 "Unlike 1998 when financial markets were rattled by a weak Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and property market, our economy is now riding on healthy retail, tourism and real estate sectors. Interest rates are also low," said Francis Kwok, director at Peace Town Securities Ltd.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, shares in Hong Kong property developer Far East Consortium International Ltd. (0035.HK) bucked the market downtrend, jumping 10.67 percent to HK$1.66 after the firm said it planned to sell a property in the heart of Kowloon for HK$468.8 million.  \par \par \uc2 Shares of ship chartering and00Jewellery chain operator Hang Fung Gold Technology Ltd. (0870.HK) tumbled 11.33 percent to HK$1.33 after the firm posted a 26 percent drop in full year earnings during the midday break.  \par \par \uc2 (US$1=HK$7.8).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040722e07m001c2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
