\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr weakens on fund outflows, HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 576 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2004\par 11:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , July 21 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar weakened\par on Wednesday as funds continued to flow out of the territory,\par forcing the de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step in three times to\par defend the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's peg to the U.S. dollar.\par     By 0920 GMT the Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) reported\par it had bought a total of HK$2.184 billion (US$280 million) worth\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollars from banks.\par     After the HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was still trading at 7.7999/7.80 per U.S. dollar at 0930 GMT\par versus HK$7.7998/99 in late Asian trade on Tuesday.\par     Under Hong Kong's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board system, the HKMA is\par committed to defending the pegged rate of HK$7.8 by buying Hong\par Kong dollars in exchange for U.S. dollars.\par     "I'm not surprised at the outflow as the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par weakened over the past weeks on the heels of wider differentials\par between Hong Kong and U.S. interest rates," one trader said.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There will be more outflows coming up."\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has suffered selling pressure recently on\par arbitrage trades, after the Fed raised rates by 25 basis points\par at the end of June but Hong Kong banks left rates unchanged.\par  \par     Another dealer said the U.S. dollar had rebounded after the\par testimony of Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Tuesday.\par     Greenspan said the U.S. economy had entered a substantial\par expansion, reinforcing expectations that U.S. interest rates\par would continue to rise at a "measured" pace.\par     "The interest rate gap will become greater if Hong Kong\par continues to lag behind the U.S. in raising rates in future,"\par another dealer from a European bank said.\par     Some dealers said Hong Kong banks might not follow the Fed's\par move unless the aggregate balance falls back to its normal level\par of less than HK$1 billion from current excessive liquidity.\par     The latest move by the HKMA will reduce the aggregate balance\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - the sum of balances on clearing accounts maintained by banks   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 with the HKMA - to HK$29.522 billion on Friday after the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 settlement of the capital outflow.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, discounts on Hong Kong dollar forwards narrowed   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 from session lows amid the fund outflows. The discount on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one-year contracts was trading around 620/600 pips,   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 versus a low of 650 pips in the afternoon and tightening from   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tuesday's close of 630/610 pips.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the cash market, mid-and longer-dated interbank rates   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 edged up further after tracking higher U.S. bond yields   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 overnight.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The one-year local rate rose to 1.49-1.52 from 1.38-1.42\par percent in the previous day.\par                    Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                    At 0942 GMT   At 0317 GMT   At 0844 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7999/7.80   7.7997/98     7.7998/99\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -234 / -229   -236 / -233   -233 / -228\par  Six-month         -407 / -397   -417 / -407   -410 / -400\par  One-year          -620 / -600   -640 / -620   -630 / -610\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight        Three-month        0.40 / 0.45  0.40 / 0.45   0.38 / 0.42\par  Six-month          0.81 / 0.86  0.80 / 0.85   0.73 / 0.77\par  One-year           1.49 / 1.54  1.47 / 1.52   1.38 / 1.42\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040721e07l000yr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
