\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar weak, HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , more outflows seen.   \b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Mai 2004\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , May 11 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar was\par under pressure on Tuesday on fears of further fund flows out of\par the territory, forcing the defacto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to step in\par three times to maintain the pegged exchange rate of 7.80 to the\par U.S. dollar.\par     The HKMA reported it bought HK$4.602 billion from banks on\par Tuesday afternoon in three moves in a bid to keep the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par steady against the U.S. dollar.\par     The authority has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  eight times in less than two\par weeks. It has bought a total of HK$5.928 billion worth of Hong\par Kong dollars since April 30, to support the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The HKMA is committed under the territory's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime\par to buy Hong Kong dollars to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if it weakens\par below 7.8 to the U.S. dollar.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has suffered selling pressure recently\par as the Hong Kong stock market has dropped on rate rise fears\par and tightening measures in China, and because the U.S. dollar\par has strengthened, making U.S.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar assets potentially more\par attractive.\par     "Funds have been flowing out of the stock market recently,"\par a dealer at a local bank said. "Investors have been selling\par China shares in the past few days on worries that Beijing may\par introduce further measures to cool its overheating economy."\par     Leading Hong Kong shares were slightly firmer on Tuesday\par though, attracting bargain hunters after a sharp sell-off on\par Monday. But some analysts believe the correction is not over\par yet.\par     The blue-chip Hang Seng Index        ended up 0.20 percent,\par while the H-share index  of China-registered companies\par listed in Hong Kong rose 1.25 percent.\par     "The local stock market is still weak. Some investors will\par continue to withdraw funds from Hong Kong," another dealer\par said.\par  \par     Hong Kong interbank rates edged up and discounts on Hong\par Kong dollar forwards narrowed after the HKMA's latest moves.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          tightened to a\par six-month high of 250/230 pips by 0924 GMT from 290/270 pips in\par offshore trade on Monday.\par     The one-year local interbank rate rose to 1.60-1.67 percent\par from Monday's close of 1.52-1.54 percent.\par                          Close       Morning  Previous Close\par                    At 0920 GMT   At 0230 GMT     At 0820 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT          7.7999/7.80   7.7999/7.80\par   7.7999/7.80\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month       -135 / -130   -143 / -138     -158 / -153\par  Six-month         -192 / -182   -215 / -205     -250 / -240\par  One-year          -250 / -230   -285 / -265     -340 / -320\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.001/0.002   0.003/0.003\par  0.001/0.003\par  Three-month       0.46 / 0.49   0.43 / 0.50     0.35 / 0.36\par  Six-month         0.93 / 0.95   0.87 / 0.96     0.78 / 0.80\par  One-year          1.60 / 1.67   1.60 / 1.65     1.52 / 1.54\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages.\par Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed\par on Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f2