\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA buys HK$390 million in exchange for US dlrs.   \b0\par\par\uc2 194 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Mai 2004\par 12:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, May 10 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary\par Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA), the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said\par on Monday it had bought HK$390 million from banks in exchange\par for U.S. dollars, in its second \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the day.\par     Under \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board system, the HKMA is\par committed to buying Hong Kong dollars in exchange for U.S.\par dollars whenever the Hong Kong unit weakens below its peg of\par 7.8 to the U.S. dollar.\par     The HKMA bought HK$156 million in exchange for U.S. dollars\par in an earlier \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Monday, giving a total\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of HK$546 million by late Monday. Real time\par information available on Reuters page  showed the\par transaction occurred at 0950 GMT.\par     The Hong Kong dollar has been under pressure recently as\par the U.S. dollar has rebounded against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par expectations of higher interest rates, making U.S. dollar\par assets potentially more attractive.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A recent correction in the Hong Kong stock market has also\par reduced demand for Hong Kong dollars and sparked concerns about\par further capital outflows from the territory.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040510e05a00157\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\p