\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr recovers slightly in wake of HKMA action.   \b0\par\par\uc2 688 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2004\par 12:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, April 30 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar\par strengthened above its peg and discounts on Hong Kong dollar\par forwards retreated from the day's high late on Friday, as some\par players took profits in the wake of HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the territory's de facto\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sold HK$156 million (US$20 million) worth of U.S.\par dollars for Hong Kong dollars on Friday afternoon, its first sale\par of the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the interbank market since September\par 2002, an HKMA spokesman said.\par  \par     The HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as fears of a funds outflow pushed the\par HKD down to its peg.\par     "There has been good demand for U.S. dollars in recent\par sessions. I think it is mainly due to China's measures to cool\par its economy," said a dealer at a local bank.\par     "I'm not ruling out there will be more outflows coming up."\par     The Hong Kong money market was jittery on Friday amid\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2  concerns that a credit tightening in mainland China will slow    \par \par \uc2  money inflows into Hong Kong, and on speculation China will raise    \par \par \uc2  interest rates.    \par \par \uc2  The South China Morning Post newspaper reported on Friday    \par \par \uc2  that China would raise commercial bank lending rates by half a    \par \par \uc2  percentage point after the week-long Labour Day holiday starting    \par \par \uc2  on May 1.    \par \par \uc2  Before the HKMA news, the local dollar  returned to its    \par \par \uc2  pegged rate of HK$7.80 to the U.S. dollar after hovering above    \par \par \uc2  this level for seven months, and discounts on forwards narrowed    \par \par \uc2  sharply from the previous session.    \par \par \uc2  "There was some selling of the U.S. dollar in the spot market    \par \par \uc2  after the HKMA report. Some profit-taking also emerged in the    \par \par \uc2  forwards market after the one-year contracts tightened by about    \par \par \uc2  100 pips during the day," one dealer said.    \par \par \uc2  By 0858 GMT, the Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7997/98 to    \par \par \uc2  the U.S. dollar, while the discount on one-year forwards    \par \par \uc2  was at 365/345 pips against an intraday high of 320 pips and    \par \par \uc2  Thursday's close of 450/430 pips.    \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong money market has also been hit recently by    \par \par \uc2  growing expectations of higher U.S. interest rates, SARS concerns    \par \par \uc2  and by a bout of weakness in the local stock market.    \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong's top share index closed below 12,000 points for    \par \par \uc2  the first time in five months on Friday, rattled by fears of    \par \par \uc2  interest rate rises in China and the United States.    \par \par \uc2  The Hang Seng Index  was down 0.52 percent, while the    \par \par \uc2  H-share index of China-incorporated companies listed in Hong Kong    \par \par \uc2  dropped  0.21 percent.    \par \par \uc2  Dealers said an outflow of funds from Hong Kong had led to a    \par \par \uc2  fall in the aggregate balance, the sum of balances on clearing    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     A decline in the aggregate balance pushes up Hong Kong\par interbank interest rates.\par     The three-month rate was quoted at 0.40-0.45 percent, rising\par from 0.18-0.24 percent on Thursday, while the one-year rate\par firmed to 1.28-1.32 percent from 1.05-1.15 percent.\par     The HKMA forecasts the aggregate balance, a key measure of\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interbank liquidity, will fall to HK$54.509 billion on Tuesday\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Friday's HK$54.665 billion after settlement of the HK$156\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                     At 0858 GMT   At 0325 GMT   At 0900 GMT\par  HK$ SPOT           7.7997/98     7.7999/7.80   7.7998/99\par  FORWARDS\par  Three-month        -142 / -137   -137 / -132   -173 / -169\par  Six-month          -245 / -235   -235 / -225   -290 / -280\par  One-year           -365 / -345   -345 / -325   -450 / -430\par  INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par  Overnight         0.0005/0.0008 0.005 / 0.01  0.0008/0.008\par  Three-month        0.40 / 0.45   0.35 / 0.40   0.18 / 0.24\par  Six-month          0.70 / 0.75   0.70 / 0.75   0.48 / 0.56\par  One-year           1.28 / 1.32   1.25 / 1.37   1.05 / 1.15\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par Reuters contributor page .\par     (US$=HK$7.8).\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040430e04u00182\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
