\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar weakens in late afternoon trade.   \b0\par\par\uc2 457 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2004\par 11:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     HONG KONG, Feb 24 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar weakened\par on Tuesday as bidding interest for the U.S. dollar against the\par local unit emerged in late afternoon session.\par     "After the London market opened, there was some buying\par interest in the spot market," said a dealer from a Japanese bank.\par     The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         was trading at 7.7777/78 at 0929\par GMT, weaker than 7.7757/59 in late Asian trade on Monday but\par still stronger than its HK$7.80 peg to the greenback.\par     "I see the spot rate possibly retesting late January's low of\par 7.7790 and then the next target is 7.78," the dealer said.\par     Another dealer said investors will gradually bid up the spot\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2  rate, saying the Hong Kong unit's recent rise against the U.S.    \par \par \uc2  dollar would be capped. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA)    \par \par \uc2  has regularly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in past months to arrest the local    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation.    \par \par \uc2  He said that the HKMA had bought U.S. dollars from banks at    \par \par \uc2  HK$7.7680 earlier this month and market players suspect it may    \par \par \uc2  want to continue to keep the exchange rate at those levels.    \par \par \uc2  Discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards widened in the morning    \par \par \uc2  on news that the United States was leading a delegation to    \par \par \uc2  Beijing this week for meetings with China's central bankers and    \par \par \uc2  others on increasing cooperation on financial issues. Market    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     But forward discounts narrowed in late afternoon in line with\par a weaker Hong Kong dollar.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          was trading at\par 655/640 pips versus 670/660 pips in late morning and Monday's\par close of 655/645 pips.\par     One dealer at a European bank said upside for the forwards\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par would be limited given abundant liquidity in the market and\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par strong resistance at around 600 pips. He expected the discount on\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one-year forwards to move between the 600 and 700 pip range in\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0918 GMT   At 0330 GMT   At 0916 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7777/79     7.7760/61     7.7757/59\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -190 / -187   -192 / -190   -188 / -185\par     Six-month        -365 / -360   -375 / -365   -368 / -358\par     One-year         -655 / -640   -670 / -660   -655 / -645\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight       0.005 / 0.01   0.001/0.005   0.01 / 0.02\par     Three-month      0.05 / 0.08   0.06 / 0.07   0.07 / 0.08\par     Six-month        0.13 / 0.17   0.13 / 0.15   0.14 / 0.16\par     One-year         0.40 / 0.48   0.42 / 0.45   0.47 / 0.49\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters contributor page .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040224e02o00191\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
