\par\par \b \uc2 HK dlr fwds discount narrows, yuan talk persists.    \b0\par\par\uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2004\par 10:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Feb 17 (Reuters) - Discounts on Hong Kong dollar\par forwards narrowed on Tuesday as some players bought back into the\par market after yesterday's sell-off on jitters over Chinese yuan\par revaluation talk.\par     "There was some profit taking in view of a narrowing in yuan\par non-deliverable forwards (NDFs). The move was also prompted by\par dollar/yen movement," said a dealer from a European bank.\par     The dollar rose against the yen on Tuesday afternoon to its\par highest level in 11 days as traders grew nervous about possible\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of Japan.\par     The discount on one-year HKD forwards          was trading\par around 710/690 pips, slightly narrower than 720/705 pips late on\par Monday.\par     But dealers said lingering speculation of yuan revaluation\par and abundant liquidity in the market were likely to keep downward\par pressure on forwards.\par  \par     "Expectations that China will adjust its fixed rate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par regime are unlikely to go away," another dealer said.\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A number of investment houses expect China to slightly widen\par the yuan's trading band from its peg to the U.S. dollar this year\par or link it to a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     In the spot market, the Hong Kong dollar edged lower on talk\par of short covering on U.S. dollar positions.\par     The Hong Kong unit        was trading at 7.7708/10 per U.S.\par dollar at 0917 GMT, weaker than 7.7685/86 in late Asian trade on\par Monday.\par     Dealers said the spot rate had been supported at around\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HK$7.7685 per U.S. dollar in recent days, near levels at which\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and they expect\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0826 GMT   At 0330 GMT   At 0852 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7705/06     7.7698/99     7.7685/86\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -197 / -193   -198 / -193   -198 / -192\par     Six-month        -385 / -381   -390 / -380   -390 / -380\par     One-year         -710 / -690   -710 / -695   -720 / -705\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight    0.00001/0.00001 0.00001/0.00001 0.00001/0.00001\par     Three-month      0.02 / 0.05   0.015 / 0.02   0.01 / 0.04\par     Six-month        0.11 / 0.14    0.08 / 0.10   0.10 / 0.13\par     One-year         0.34 / 0.43    0.35 / 0.37   0.37 / 0.42\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters contributor page .\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040217e02h001nn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
