\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar eases on short US dollar covering.    \b0\par\par\uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2004\par 11:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     HONG KONG, Feb 13 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar weakened\par slightly against the U.S. unit on Friday as some players\par covered their short U.S. dollars positions, dealers said.\par     "There is some short covering of U.S. dollar. People are\par locking in profits in the spot and forwards markets," said a\par dealer from a local bank.\par     Dealers said the spot rate has been bid up in London trade\par on Thursday.\par     "A big U.S. house bid up the spot rate late on Thursday\par afternoon for unknown reasons, although players believe that it\par might be related to short covering," another trader said.\par     "Today, there was still some buying interest in the U.S.\par dollar against the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but the market was less\par volatile than yesterday," he added.\par     The Hong Kong unit        shuffled between 7.7700 and\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7.7715 per U.S. dollar throughout the day. It was trading at    \f28 \par \par \uc2 7.7706/08 per U.S. dollar at 0922 GMT, compared with Thursday's    \par \par \uc2 low of 7.7725 in London trade and New York's close of around    \par \par \uc2 7.77 on Thursday.    \par \par \uc2 There was speculation that buying interest in the U.S.    \par \par \uc2 dollar came after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority intervened\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 in the market earlier this week, buying U.S. dollars from banks    \par \par \uc2 at HK$7.7680 in a bid to curb the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.    \par \par \uc2 "Some market players bid up the spot rate as they saw    \par \par \uc2 limited upside for the Hong Kong dollar...I think the    \par \par \uc2 resistance will be HK$7.7730," one dealer at a European bank    \par \par \uc2 said.    \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar strengthened markedly late last year    \par \par \uc2 as the local economy began to improve and speculation grew that    \par \par \uc2 China might adjust its fixed rate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime.     \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Meanwhile, the Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound in\par thin trade, dealers said.\par     "There was not too much trading interest in the market. The\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 discount on one-year forwards has been trading in a relatively    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 tight range of 680 and 650 pips in recent days," the European    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bank dealer said.     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     He expects the forwards to move between -700 and -600 in\par the coming weeks and to track the spot market.\par     By late afternoon, the discount on one-year forwards\par   was quoted at 670/650 pips versus Thursday's 670/660\par pips.\par                      Close         Late Morning  Previous Close\par                      At 0850 GMT   At 0455 GMT   At 0854 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7706/09     7.7707/08     7.7695/7.77\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -193 / -191   -196 / -191   -195 / -190\par     Six-month        -375 / -370   -376 / -366   -378 / -370\par     One-year         -670 / -650   -660 / -650   -680 / -670\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight       0.00/0.00001 0.00001/0.00003\par 0.00001/0.00003\par     Three-month      0.03 / 0.04   0.03 / 0.05   0.02 / 0.05\par     Six-month        0.12 / 0.14   0.11 / 0.14   0.11 / 0.14\par     One-year         0.40 / 0.44   0.43 / 0.45   0.34 / 0.46\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages.\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Live quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 on Reuters contributor