\par\par \b \uc2 Hong Kong dollar firms after Greenspan's remarks.    \b0\par\par\uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2004\par 10:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Feb 12 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar edged\par higher on Thursday, buoyed by overnight comments from U.S.\par Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan that played down the\par prospect of an early U.S. rate rise, pulling the greenback down\par against the euro and major Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par     Greenspan, in his semi-annual report on monetary policy to\par the House of Representatives Financial Services Committee, said\par on Wednesday there was no rush to raise interest rates and that a\par weak U.S. dollar would narrow the wide U.S. current account gap.\par     The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2         shuffled between 7.7685 and\par 7.77 per U.S. dollar throughout the day. It was trading at\par 7.7695/7.77 at 0854 GMT, firmer than 7.7708/09 in late Asian\par trade on Wednesday.\par     But dealers said the Hong Kong unit's rise against the\par weakened U.S.\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar would be capped, as it is pegged to the\par greenback at 7.8 and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par regularly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to arrest the local dollar's appreciation.\par     "After the HKMA bought U.S. dollars from banks at HK$7.7680\par recently, market players suspect it may want to keep the exchange\par rate at those levels. So they will think twice before taking\par positions."\par     The territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold HK$544 million and\par bought U.S. dollars in offshore markets on Tuesday in a bid to\par curb the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise.\par     Dealers said the HKMA has been gradually adjusting its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  level from 7.7630, 7.7640 to 7.7680 in recent weeks.\par They see no let up in further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as more funds are\par expected to flow into Asia on the heels of U.S. dollar weakness\par and persistent speculation about Chinese yuan appreciation.\par  \par     Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound but the discounts\par on longer-dated contracts widened the most, dealers said.\par     "Shorter-dated forwards didn't move much on ample liquidity\par in the market, and front-end interbank rates remained close to\par zero," one dealer said.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          was quoted at\par 680/670 pips, widening from Wednesday's close of 660/650 pips.\par     In the cash market, most interbank rates fell. The one-year\par local rate was quoted at 0.34-0.46 percent, down from 0.49-0.51\par percent.\par                      Close         Morning        Previous Close\par                      At 0854 GMT   At 0300 GMT    At 0850 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7695/7.77   7.7689/90      7.7703/04\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -195 / -190   -195 / -190    -194 / -190\par     Six-month        -378 / -370   -380 / -370    -375 / -365\par     One-year         -680 / -670   -680 / -665    -660 / -650\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight    0.00001/0.00003 0.00003/0.0005  0.00008/0.0001\par     Three-month      0.02 / 0.05   0.02 / 0.04    0.03 / 0.05\par     Six-month        0.11 / 0.14   0.10 / 0.12    0.14 / 0.17\par     One-year         0.34 / 0.46   0.38 / 0.41    0.49 / 0.51\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be 