\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar steady after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2004\par 05:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Jan 28 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar was stable\par on Wednesday morning after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  overnight to stem the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise against the U.S.\par dollar.\par     Data showing Americans were still having a tough time finding\par jobs depressed the U.S. dollar and prompted some switching into\par Hong Kong dollars.\par     Meanwhile, the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to strengthen on\par strong fund flows into Hong Kong, including the stock market\par which hit a 19-month closing high on Tuesday and drew a hefty\par HK$24.6 billion (US$3.2 billion) in turnover.\par  The HKMA sold around US$250 million late on Tuesday and\par overnight in three \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unit was\par trading at HK$7.7649 in late morning.\par  \par     "It's steady at 7.7649, after hitting HK$7.7630, so I don't\par expect any more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  today," said one trader.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unit is pegged to the U.S. dollar at HK$7.8 but\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strengthened markedly late last year as the local economy began   \f28 \par \par \uc2 to improve and speculation grew that China might adjust its fixed   \par \par \uc2 rate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The discount on one-year forwards          were trading at\par around 650/640 pips, versus 620/600 pips late on Tuesday.\par                      Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0344 GMT   At 0845 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7649        7.7663/66\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -195 / -193   -191.5 / -190.5\par     Six-month        -370 / -363   -362 / -359\par     One-year         -650 / -640   -620 / -600\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.001/0.0001   0.005/0.001\par     Three-month      0.06 / 0.03   0.08/0.05\par     Six-month        0.16 / 0.13   0.20/0.15\par     One-year         0.50 / 0.45   0.53/0.48\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040128e01s000q4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
