\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA's Yam says no limit on HK dlr  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2004\par 06:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 19 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has repeatedly sold local dollars in the recent months to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said on Monday there was no limit on the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed.    \par \par \uc2  "There are, of course, large numbers (of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) but there is no limit as to how large they can become," HKMA Chief Executive Joseph Yam told a luncheon.    \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to the U.S. dollar at HK$7.80 per dollar.    \par \par \uc2  But the HKMA has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly since late September to keep it close to that level, buying U.S. dollars and selling local dollars.    \par \par \uc2  The Hong Kong dollar has strengthened amid strong demand from overseas investors as the local stock market rallies and the territory's economic recovery accelerates.    \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to remain strong in anticipation of more 'hot money' flowing into the territory, given that a number of Chinese firms are planning initial public offerings on the Hong Kong bourse this year.    \par \par \uc2  The local unit  eased to 7.7660/61 at 0350 GMT on Monday morning, compared with 7.7632/33 on Friday in Asian trade.    \par \par \uc2  Yam said the HKMA's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have totalled US$6.7 billion.    \par \par \uc2  "There is no limit to the amount of domestic money that can be created if the demand is there," he said.    \par \par \uc2  The HKMA could issue more exchange fund paper to mop up a large pool of Hong Kong dollars in the aggregate balance.    \par \par \uc2  "(We have) an open mind on this possibility," Yam said.    \par \par \uc2  He also said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability is essential to the proper function of the economy and monetary policy.    \par \par \uc2  Speculation that China will widen its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band has also prompted some players to take positios on the Hong Kong dollar.    \par \par \uc2  But Yam said he did not see the need for an appreciation of China's yuan exchange rate.    \par \par \uc2  China is running a current account surplus, which is less than one percent of gross domestic product, and is shrinking under the influence of the World Trade Organisation, indicating that there is nothing fundamentally wrong with the level of its exchange rate, he said.    \par \par \uc2  "There is no need to mess around with the exchange rate," he added.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040119e01j000uv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
