\par\par \b \uc2 Fund flows buoy HK dlr but  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  fears weigh.   \b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 2004\par 04:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Jan 9 (Reuters) - Strong capital inflows continued\par to keep the Hong Kong dollar firm on Friday morning but movements\par were limited by fears of further \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the territory's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "The economy is recovering, the political environment here is\par far more stable than in the United States and other places, so\par funds are coming in," a dealer at a European bank said.\par     Hong Kong's economic recovery appears to be accelerating,\par aided by a string of economic incentives from Beijing and a\par rebound in consumer confidenc, fuelled in part by a prolonged\par rally in share prices.\par     Foreign funds has been flowing into Hong Kong stocks, pushing\par the benchmark stock index to fresh two-and-a-half year highs in\par heavy turnover.\par     Leading Hong Kong stocks were up nearly one percent late on\par Friday morning and appeared poised to extend their latest winning\par streak to a tenth consecutive day.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The local unit        was trading at 7.7632/33 at 0330 GMT,\par little changed from 7.7630/31 on Thursday.\par     The Hong Kong dollar strengthened suddenly above its peg of\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 7.80 to the U.S. unit in September. The Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary   \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA), the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has been   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regularly since then and had sold a total of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HK$11.451 billion this week in a bid to curb the local unit's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 strength.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The latest HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  lifted the aggregate balance -   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 a key measure of interbank liquidity - to HK$43.898 billion on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Monday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The discount on Hong Kong dollar forwards widened slightly   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 and interbank interest rates softened on Friday in the face of   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 rising interbank liquidity, dealers said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The discount on one-year forwards widened to 745/725   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pips from 730/710 pips. The discount on two-year forwards   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 was quoted at 1050/900 pips.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Short-term interbank rates remained near zero, while the   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 one-year rate eased to 0.40-0.45 percent from Thursday's   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0.43-0.46 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dealers said the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to remain strong   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in anticipation of more 'hot money' flowing into the territory   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 given that a number of Chinese companies are planning initial   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 public offerings on the Hong Kong bourse this year.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     They include Ping An Insurance, China Construction Bank,\par Minsheng Bank and Air China.\par                      Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0330 GMT   At 0919 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7632/33     7.7630/31\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -202 / -195   -203 / -195\par     Six-month        -390 / -380   -388 / -378\par     One-year         -745 / -725   