\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  keep traders wary, dollar steady.   \b0\par\par\uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 2004\par 05:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Jan 8 (Reuters) - The Hong Kong dollar cautiously\par stuck to its recent range on Thursday morning after numerous\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) in\par recent sessions, but dealers said upward pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par has not abated.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par four times on Wednesday during onshore and offshore trading,\par selling a total of HK$4.332 billion and buying U.S. dollars in an\par effort to curb the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise.\par     "The spot rate didn't move much after aggressive HKMA\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . That implies there is still strong selling of U.S.\par dollars and robust demand for Hong Kong dollars," one trader\par said.\par  \par     "The local economy is recovering with a booming stock market\par that is attracting foreign fund flows," the dealer said.\par     The Hong Kong dollar        was trading at 7.7630/31 at 0330\par GMT, little changed from 7.7632/22 late on Wednesday.\par     The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to the U.S. unit at 7.80, but\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 has been under upward pressure since September on speculation   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 about a revaluation of the Chinese yuan, brighter domestic   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 economic prospects and capital inflows.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Hong Kong will release retail sales data for November on\par Thursday afternoon.\par     Sales were likely boosted by improving consumer confidence,\par Christmas shopping and a steady stream of tourists from mainland\par China but markets are unlikely to react to the lagging indicator.\par     Hong Kong dollar forwards were rangebound.\par     "The discount on longer-dated forwards narrowed in early\par trade on short covering before selling emerged," said a dealer\par from a European bank.\par     "In the long term, a widening bias for the forwards remains\par given a large aggregate balance and the market expects a possible\par revaluation of Chinese yuan," the dealer said.\par     After a string of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the HKMA in recent months,\par the aggregate balance -- a key measure of interbank liquidity --\par will increase to HK$41.313 billion on Friday.\par     Speculation persisted in the market that Beijing would widen\par the yuan trading band or revalue the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year, traders\par said.\par     Some investors are betting that such moves would prompt a\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 revaluation of the Hong Kong dollar, as the two economies have   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 become increasingly more closely interwined since the former   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 British colony returned to Chinese rule in 1997.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China has shrugged off calls from the United States and other   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 countries to revalue the yuan, which is pegged in a narrow range   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 around 8.28 to the dollar, but has pledged long-term reform to   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  regime.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. and Chinese officials are expected to meet in Beijing   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 this month to discuss U.S. demands that China liberalise its   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The discount on one-year forwards was trading around   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 720/700 pips by midday, versus 680 pips in early trade and   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 725/705 late on Wednesday.    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                      Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0330 GMT   At 0832 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7630/31     7.7631/32\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -200 / -195   -205 / -200\par     Six-month        -380 / -370   -385 / -375\par     One-year         -720 / -700   -725 / -705\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.001/0.002   0.004/0.005\par     Three-month      0.04 / 0.06   0.05 / 0.07\par     Six-month        0.13 / 0.15   0.10 / 0.12\par     One-year         0.43 / 0.45   0.43 / 0.45\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reuters contributor page .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040108e018000ms\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
