\par\par \b \uc2 HKMA sells HK$777 mln in third  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 158 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Januar 2004\par 02:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 HONG KONG\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 7 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  (HKMA), the territory's de facto \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the money markets for a third time on Wednesday, selling HK$777 million and buying U.S. dollars in an effort to stabilise the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA has sold HK$4.27 billion in three \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday morning, according to real time information available on Reuters .  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar was trading at 7.7630/31 at 0134 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 The HKMA sold HK$505 million on Monday and a further HK$4.06 billion on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to the U.S. dollar at HK$7.80 per dollar. However, the HKMA has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent months to keep it close to that level and offset strong demand for Hong Kong dollars amid growing signs of economic recovery in the territory.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040107e017000bf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
