\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar remains strong as more fund inflows seen.   \b0\par\par\uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2004\par 11:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     HONG KONG, Jan 6 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar remained\par stubbornly strong on Tuesday despite repeated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) to weaken it, riding\par higher with other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on U.S. dollar weakness.\par     The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to the U.S. unit at 7.8 but it\par has been chafing against this in recent months, buoyed by an\par improving local economy, a booming stock market and foreign fund\par inflows.\par     "As long as the U.S. dollar remains weak with low interest\par rates against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the upward pressure on the Hong\par Kong dollar is likely to persist," said a dealer from a European\par bank.\par     The greenback continued to fall on Tuesday, skidding to a\par record low against the euro and plumbing a fresh 11-year trough\par versus the British pound on worries about a festering U.S.\par current account deficit and U.S. interest rates.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said strong gains for Hong Kong stocks and a flurry\par of upcoming initial public offerings have fuelled an inflow of\par funds and demand for the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Top Hong Kong shares ended higher for the seventh straight\par session on Tuesday as investors bet on stronger local economic\par growth. The benchmark Hang Seng Index  ended 0.24 percent\par higher at 13,036.32.\par     The HKMA sold HK$1.941 billion and bought U.S. dollars in\par three separate moves on Tuesday in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , following up on\par overnight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . It sold a total of HK$505 million in two\par separate moves during offshore trading overnight.\par     The latest move will further boost the aggregate balance -- a\par key measure of interbank liquidity -- to a new high of HK$34.862\par billion on Thursday.\par     After the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar exchange\par rate  was trading at HK$7.7630/32 at 0923 GMT, compared\par with 7.7638/40 late on Monday.\par     Discounts on Hong Kong dollar forwards deepened and interbank\par interest rates softened further in view of the rising interbank\par liquidity.\par     "I think the Hong Kong dollar forwards discounts widened in\par reaction to the HKMA injections and a softening in Chinese yuan\par non-deliverable forwards (NDF)," said a dealer from a Japanese\par bank.\par     U.S. and Chinese officials are expected to meet in Beijing in\par January to discuss U.S. demands that China liberalise its\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . There has been speculation the Hong Kong unit may move\par in tandem with the yuan should the latter be revalued.\par     Hong Kong, a former British colony, has been forging closer\par economic ties with mainland China since it reverted to Chinese\par rule in 1997.\par     In the cash market, short-term interbank rates remained near\par zero, while the one-year rate eased to 0.57-0.60 percent from\par Monday's close of 0.65-0.67 percent.\par  \par                      Close         Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0930 GMT   At 0330 GMT   At 0845 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7630/32     7.7630/31     7.7639/41