\par\par \b \uc2 HK dollar remains strong despite HKMA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2004\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 HONG KONG\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Jan 6 (Reuters) - The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar remained\par strong on Tuesday morning despite a concerted round of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (HKMA) to weaken\par it, supported by U.S. dollar weakness and bullish sentiment in\par Hong Kong's stock market.\par     The HKMA, the territory's de facto \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par on Tuesday morning for the third time in 24 hours in a bid to\par rein in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength.\par     It sold HK$776 million and bought U.S. dollars in addition to\par selling HK$505 million in two separate moves during offshore\par trading overnight.\par     The latest move will further boost the aggregate balance -- a\par key measure of interbank liquidity -- to a new high of HK$33.697\par billion on Thursday.\par     After the latest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar exchange\par rate  was trading at HK$7.7630/31 at 0333 GMT, compared\par with 7.7638/40 late on Monday.\par  \par     "Funds are flowing to Asian markets given weakness in the\par U.S.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar," said a dealer from a European bank.\par     The greenback was dangling near recent multi-year lows\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Tuesday, weighed down by a festering\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. trade gap and the prospect of U.S. interest rates remaining\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par low.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said strong gains for Hong Kong stocks had also\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fuelled an inflow of funds. However, they see a risk of further\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HKMA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the near term.\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Discounts on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hong Kong\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar forwards deepened and interbank\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interest rates softened further in view of the rising interbank\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "Selling in longer-dated forwards was aggressive due to low\par short-term rates," another trader from a European bank said.\par     The discount on one-year forwards          widened to 680/660\par pips from 600/590 pips late on Monday.\par     Short-term interbank rates remained near zero, while the\par one-year rate eased to 0.60-0.65 percent from Monday's close of\par 0.65-0.67 percent.\par     Hong Kong Chief Executive Tung Chee-hwa will deliver his\par annual policy address on Wednesday but dealers do not expect Tung\par to surprise.\par     "People don't expect him to do much but they will want to\par hear about what else mainland China will do to help Hong Kong\par further," one dealer said.\par     Hong Kong's economy has begun to pick up in recent months,\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aided by a string of economic incentives from Beijing. These\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par include the lifting of restrictions on individual mainland\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par visitors coming to Hong Kong, a landmark free trade deal and\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par              Morning       Previous Close\par                      At 0330 GMT   At 0845 GMT\par     HK$ SPOT         7.7630/31     7.7639/41\par     FORWARDS\par     Three-month      -195 / -190   -190 / -187\par     Six-month        -380 / -370   -360 / -350\par     One-year         -680 / -660   -600 / -590\par     INTERBANK RATE (PERCENTAGE)\par     Overnight        0.001/0.002   0.001/0.001\par     Three-month      0.07 / 0.11   0.09 / 0.11\par     Six-month        0.20 / 0.25   0.20 / 0.22\par     One-year         0.60 / 0.65   0.65 / 0.67\par     Source: Indicative quotes were taken from Reuters pages. Live\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quotes for both Forwards and Interbank Rates can be viewed on\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters contributor page .\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040106e016001bv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
